<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Culture &amp; Lifestyle</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-cul</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:55Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-cul" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1441?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-cul" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Who was Eva Mamlok? Berlin square renamed after Jewish anti-fascist resistance fighter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db08b2188c296d6ebad867cb1799c3061c6f5c5d52f1abc60ba694f767fccc34</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T09:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-was-eva-mamlok-berlin-square-renamed-after-jewish-anti-fascist-resistance-fighter/a-79668919--fa371a8e7f27.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-was-eva-mamlok-berlin-square-renamed-after-jewish-anti-fascist-resistance-fighter/a-79668919?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She started taking action against Hitler as a teenager and never stopped until her death in a concentration camp. Berlin's Blücherplatz is now being renamed after her.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>German lawmakers back monthly state pension contributions for children, with families able to add more.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:42220734849f06cbaa6cb17b6319215b44170c10e90079367d0b88b7d9ad7644</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T11:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-lawmakers-back-monthly-state-pension-contributions-for-children-with-families-able-to-add-mor/live-79678671--02713419dab3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-lawmakers-back-monthly-state-pension-contributions-for-children-with-families-able-to-add-more/live-79678671?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's parliament has backed a plan to help children save for retirement from the age of 6. Meanwhile, Jewish students report death threats after they confronted a far-right lawmaker.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>AI-assisted dying? Doris Dörrie's new film addresses prospect of care robots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:15bc992553f8d6f6ba4824ce64e94482ce8e08280790398b48f50194cea87b4f</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T13:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-assisted-dying-doris-d_rrie-s-new-film-addresses-prospect-of-care-robots/a-79659715--50ff40522ded.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-assisted-dying-doris-dörrie-s-new-film-addresses-prospect-of-care-robots/a-79659715?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While the world debates the dangers of artificial intelligence, filmmaker Doris Dörrie explores how humanoid robots could change the way we deal with aging, caregiving and how people choose to die.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>China's influence in the gaming industry is growing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36d5c11d1743691067c71f7630be7aa5a0d55643c90466044765b299ae377d7b</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T11:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-influence-in-the-gaming-industry-is-growing/a-79484755--447380e7608a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-influence-in-the-gaming-industry-is-growing/a-79484755?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Home to more than 700 million gamers, China is the world's largest gaming market — but it's also one of the most tightly regulated. The effects reach far beyond China, impacting players around the world.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>UK students call for school uniforms to be banned in pornography</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56a476a6ea5ad2cfa8e496eb6b8050a61638ae39e9d71ac890ab6191ec8af9df</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T07:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-students-call-for-school-uniforms-to-be-banned-in-pornography/a-79554324--e21f080b6070.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-students-call-for-school-uniforms-to-be-banned-in-pornography/a-79554324?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Short skirts, knee-high socks, white blouses: Girls' school uniform items are widely used as costumes in pornographic videos. As students experience harassment, a group wants to change that.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>125 years of Thomas Mann's 'Buddenbrooks'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:228a88072373da80702232c535f3adf99f25af8fceb4111b30819e1da5ca3776</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T08:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/125-years-of-thomas-mann-s-buddenbrooks/a-44107236--20da98f1ab2b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/125-years-of-thomas-mann-s-buddenbrooks/a-44107236?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">This over 1,000-page masterpiece offers a panoramic view of society in the 19th century and exposes the collapse of a merchant family: unrecognized sons, disillusioned daughters and the loss of middle-class ideals.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Why music in Iran is more than just entertainment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a7212532eb1eca78aee2fd8c7eeafeca2ef1c51dec710fa975959e54118e68e</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T05:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-music-in-iran-is-more-than-just-entertainment/a-79583224--67cbee1305a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-music-in-iran-is-more-than-just-entertainment/a-79583224?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iranian authorities are trying to persuade prominent singers in exile to return home. While the state seeks to harness music as a political tool, music has also become a powerful expression of dissent and resistance.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nobel Prize in literature: How the winner is secretly chosen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e535f6ba926f8cc6f897f395c8c0cd2f63527b7455ee53447544fc3dce8ea8d</id><updated>2026-10-17T04:41:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-literature-how-the-winner-is-secretly-chosen/a-79564151--0152f72654ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-literature-how-the-winner-is-secretly-chosen/a-79564151?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Can Xue is considered one of this year's favorites; Margaret Atwood and Salman Rushdie are other strong contenders. But what goes on behind the scenes in the selection of the Nobel Prize in literature?</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
